{title: Make Faithfulness Your Pasture}
{subtitle: Psalms 37:3–4}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Cm7] | [Ab] |
| [Bbsus4] [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Do not burn [Eb]with anger over [Gm7/D]evildoers
Do not en[Cm7]vy those who do [Abmaj7]wrong
For [Fm7]like grass they will soon wither
And [Bbsus4]fade like the green [Bb]of new [Eb]growth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Trust in the [Ab]LORD and do [Bb]good
Dwell in the [Eb]land and make [Bb/D]faithfulness your pas[Cm7]ture
Take your de[Ab]light in the [Bbsus4]LORD
And he will [Bb]give you what your heart [Eb]asks
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Make faithfulness your [Ab]pasture
[Bb]Trust in the [Eb]LORD [Bb/D]and do [Cm7]good
Dwell in the [Ab]land with steady [Bb]heart
And he will give you what your heart [Eb]asks
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Commit your way to the [Bb/D]LORD
Trust in [Cm7]him and he will [Ab]act
[Fm7]He will bring out your righteousness
[Bb]Like the light and your justice [Eb]like the noonday sun
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Be still before the [Bb]LORD
And wait [Eb]patiently [Bb/D]for him [Cm7]
Do not [Ab]burn with anger over the one [Bb]
Whose way [Ab]prospers and carries out his [Bb]schemes
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Trust in [Ab]the LORD and do [Bb]good
Make faithfulness [Ab]your pasture [Bbsus4][Eb]
{end_of_verse}
